Since the list of paragraphs is not specified, a general method is applied:
- For each paragraph, identify the citation_focus_text (the part that references existing datasets, prior work, or citations).
- Calculate the technical percentage as:  
  \[
  \text{technical\_percentage} = 100\% - \left( \frac{\text{length of citation\_focus\_text}}{\text{total length of paragraph}} \right) \times 100
  \]
- The technical percentage represents the portion of the paragraph that is original, new, or not based on prior work.

